# ---------------- Matchups.events (Task 23 Part B) ----------------
# Which unit type can hit which. One global per pair, named
# <Attacker>CanAttack<Defender>: `set LandCanAttackAir to true` lets ground units shoot at
# aircraft. `me can attack other` asks this table, and the runtime asks it too — a "damage"
# or "hurt" message between two types that cannot fight never reaches the target's sheet,
# so a mismatched attack does nothing.
#
# The values below are the engine's built-in defaults written out, so this file is the place
# to retune the table: a land/air/sea RTS usually lets ground units hit air only when the
# attacker carries an anti-air weapon (per-type rows, e.g. `set MarineCanAttackAir to true`,
# arrive with the enemy-type work — this table is per unit type).
#
# SETUP (optional): nothing attaches this file. EventsManager reads it by name once per load,
# so the table is settled before the first shot; attach a sheet to it only if a game wants
# the same numbers as runnable events.

when game starts
  # ---- ground units: fight ground and sea, never the sky ----
  set LandCanAttackLand to true
  set LandCanAttackSea to true
  set LandCanAttackAir to false

  # ---- sea units: fight sea and land, never the sky ----
  set SeaCanAttackSea to true
  set SeaCanAttackLand to true
  set SeaCanAttackAir to false

  # ---- air units: fight everything, including other aircraft ----
  set AirCanAttackAir to true
  set AirCanAttackLand to true
  set AirCanAttackSea to true
